    "description": "Show the developer a short card explaining what changed on this branch: a headline, one-line changes grouped by intent, where to look first, and what was not checked. Use it when they run /changes or ask what you (or another agent) changed. Read the diffs that matter (biggest churn and public surfaces first) and use what you know from this session about why. Group by intent, not by file: one change is one thing a person would say out loud. Lead with what matters most. Every changed file must sit under a change; a path ending in \"/\" covers a folder, and small leftovers go in one \"chore\". look: at most 3 places a reviewer must check first (data that could be lost, a trust boundary, a contract that changed, anything you were unsure of); none is fine. unchecked: what nobody ran or tested, plainly. The tool refuses long text: say less, not more. After the card is shown, reply with one line pointing at the Changes pane; do not repeat the card in chat."
